ut a few cuts and bruises  here we're talking about injuries that  required serious medical attention  nevertheless as a result of intense  training incredible dedication and firm  guidance from both all might and Gran  Torino Deku eventually learned how to  control how much of one for all's power  he uses when he attacks and he learned  how to use his Quirk effectively without  constantly injuring himself when Deku  finally Masters the use of his quirk in  a way that allows him to stay out of the  hospital he is able to practice with it  and discover its true potential and  insane versatility one for all gives  Deku the ability to release enormous  amounts of stockpiled raw power which  effectively gives him super strength and  super speed as well as superhuman  agility and durability the user can  control what percentage of this  stockpiled power is released at any  given time he can focus more power  within certain parts of his body if he  chooses such as an arm or a leg or he  can just choose to distribute all the  power throughout his body as I mentioned  earlier one for all in the present time  is much stronger than it was initially  because it has been stockpiling more and  more power over the course of many  decades which means that Deku now has  access to way more power than some of  the former one for all users Deku is  also the first and only user who is able  to unlock the quirks of all the former  one for all users it turns out that the  core of the one for all Quirk had fused  with the Quirk factors of all the  previous one for all users who actually  had their own Quirk and this means that  Deku is eventually able to gain access  to six other quirks in addition to one  for all itself there have been nine one  for all users all together but since  Deco and all might are quirkless and the  first user yoichi was the original one  for all user there are six other users  whose quirk's Deku is able to unlock we  don't know why exactly Deku is the only  one 