 could hardly even recognize gear  shift when he saw Deku using it in the  present time The Quirk is just so much  stronger now that it's practically  unrecognizable and not only are all  these quirks stronger but they can also  be combined in extremely effective ways  for example combining float with one for  all's ability to propel Yourself by  unleashing an incredible amount of power  turns what is essentially levitation  into high speed flight smoke screen can  be combined with danger sense to  completely obstruct your opponent's  Vision while you still have a good idea  of what's going on thanks to Danger  sense and not only can the separate  effects of different quirks be combined  but multiple completely different quirks  can actually create brand new super  moves for instance black whip can be  paired with fajin to create a new super  move called black chain once we get to  the final Arc of the story Deku is  already extremely skilled in combining  his seven different quirks on the  battlefield and he seems to be only  getting better at this as the manga  approaches its conclusion nevertheless  even this ability to use and masterfully  combine seven different quirks may not  be the end of one for all's evolution in  fact I think that horikoshi has been  hinting that one for all is about to  undergo yet another major Evolution ever  since chapter  166 of the manga so over 200 chapters  ago as of the making of this video I am  referring to the Quirk Singularity  Theory also known as The Quirk  Singularity doomsday Theory and the  Paranormal Singularity Theory this  theory was first developed some 70 years  ago by Dr Hyundai garaki also known as  Dr ujiko it states that as time passes  and different Quirk users reproduce with  each other the quirks of their children  will blend together the quirks of the  parents and evolve even further creating  much more powerful and complex quirks  eventually these quirks will become so  overwhelmingly powerful that they will  be difficult for their users to control  and that's because the human body  doesn't evolve as quickly as quirks do  meaning that a normal human body simply  cannot handle such powerful new quirks  one day children will be born with  quirks that are unbelievably strong and  impossible for their bodies to control  and this will eventually lead to a  doomsday scenario where everyone becomes  a threat to everyone else and Chaos  ensues horikoshi has deliberately placed  on emphasis on the fact that kids in the  world of mha seem to be getting stronger  and possess even more powerful quirks  than the older Generations which was of  course an early hint that The Quirk  Singularity theory has real Merit Eddie  in particular was a crucial early  example of the rapid and dangerous  evolution of quirks her Quirk rewind is  completely different from the quirks  possessed by both of her parents it is  not just some basic blending of their  two quirks it is an outright Evolution  and because rewind manifested when Arie  was still just a child she accidentally  rewound her own father out of existence  and there was nothing that she or anyone  else could do about it the Quirk  Singularity theory stipulates that cases  like Arie are just the beginning and in  the future such cases will become more  and more common and more and more  dangerous so hints about Quirk  Singularity have been there for a very  long time but the theory was practically  confirmed to be true in chapter  347. that is when shigaraki reveals a  strange new ability that he is able to  use even while all of his quirks are  actively being erased by monoma and  Eraserhead after undergoing a bunch of  experimental procedures on his body in  order to allow his body to accommodate a  myriad of different quirks including all  for one shigaraki's body his very flesh  begins to mutate independently of the  effects of any single Quirk this  mutation takes the form of scores of  giant fingers first sprouting on one of  